{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_adapter", "label": "prom-client adapter", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_promclientregistry", "label": "promClientRegistry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns a MetricsRegistry that writes straight through to prom-client, so one scrape endpoint emits framework and application metrics together. Use it when you already run prom-client; otherwise prefer the framework native exporter and skip the dependency."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_promclientadapteroptions", "label": "PromClientAdapterOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "client and registry are mandatory - the bridge has nothing to publish into without them - plus an optional name prefix and the per-family cap."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_write_through_bridge", "label": "Write-through bridge", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every framework counter, gauge and histogram mutation lands in the prom-client registry synchronously: no background sync, no interval and no second copy of the values. prom-client holds the canonical state and the existing metrics route emits everything."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_bridge_cardinality_cap", "label": "Bridge cardinality cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The bridge needs the cap more urgently than the in-process registry: prom-client mints a series inside its own metric on every labels call and never expires one, so an unbounded label grows resident memory rather than only the scrape body. Past the cap the bridge rewrites the tuple to the family own declared label names with every value set to the overflow marker - reusing the declared names is not cosmetic, because prom-client fixes label names at construction and would throw on the very call meant to contain the damage."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_peer_dependency", "label": "prom-client peer dependency", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only required if you use this adapter."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_adapter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_promclientregistry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_adapter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_promclientadapteroptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_adapter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_write_through_bridge", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_adapter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_bridge_cardinality_cap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_adapter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_prom_client_peer_dependency", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_write_through_bridge", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_promclientregistry", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/prom-client-adapter.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_bridge_cardinality_cap", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_prom_client_adapter_promclientregistry", "relat